      "key":"optimisation_scope_and_reentry",
      "statement":"The opened area should be improved, subject to constitutional truth, ownership evidence and equivalence. Lawful optimisation must be boundary-local, behaviour-preserving, authority-neutral, visibility-neutral and effect-neutral. Removing local parser re-entry, consolidating local routes, improving a local algorithm/scan, or simplifying proof fixtures/tests without changing module claims can qualify. Cross-module lookup/index/cache/persistence repricing, changed public carriers/visibility/truth ownership, wider effects or observability doctrine, and performance changes to Product expectations require explicit design re-entry. Cross-boundary discoveries remain repricing inputs; admitted follow-up enters separately at the smallest lawful re-entry point. TICKETS, not this scope rule, owns follow-up recording and ticket closure effects.",
