      "key":"recurrence_threshold_and_closure",
      "statement":"Treat recurrence as a commonisation candidate. TICKETS §6 owns the rule of two, third-rebuild threshold, commonisation order and library_usage/governing_library/library_rationale fields for every implementation migration ticket. For design conformance a third rebuild must consume a reusable surface, extend it before local implementation lands, or record the stated exception. Tenant-local authority-neutral reusable patterns should be extracted. Changes to ownership, public carriers, module boundaries or shared common law are separate design decisions. Commonisation closes only when the selected path consumes the accepted relation and superseded production responsibility is retired or satisfies SPEC_METHOD §7 retention. Compare removed work and maintained responsibilities across the path; names, line count and unused helpers prove no contraction.",
